{"agent_image": null, "agent_image_digest": null, "agent_mode": null, "anthropic_pin": "2.0.50", "binary_hash_source": "post_hoc_disk", "binary_path": "/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode", "binary_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "binary_source": null, "build_channel": "local:build.ts", "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_image": "h2-env:1022@sha256:<REDACTED_HEX>", "cell_seed": 15703517891077672133, "checker_defect": false, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_lock": null, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "", "checker_timeout_s": 120, "checker_wall_time_s": 4.136, "checker_workspace_files": {".ruff_cache/.gitignore": {"bytes": 35, "mtime": 1794546782.6444547, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, ".ruff_cache/0.12.5/12745792397471449131": {"bytes": 118, "mtime": 1794546793.3525903, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, ".ruff_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG": {"bytes": 43, "mtime": 1794546782.6444547, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "check.py": {"bytes": 4412, "mtime": 1793746358.705186, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "gen.py": {"bytes": 6059, "mtime": 1794546782.676455, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "re.json": {"bytes": 400455, "mtime": 1794546796.4336293, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}, "test.py": {"bytes": 1710, "mtime": 1794547945.429108, "sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode", "run", "--print-logs", "-m", "anthropic/claude-opus-5-5", "--format", "json", "--title", "openbench", "Write a JSON file called /tmp/obench-cell-5s01n37h/bench_opencode_regex-chess_huwbm710/re.json that is a list of [regex, replacement] pairs. When executed in order with the Python code\n```\ndef all_legal_next_positions(fen):\n  for pattern, repl in json.load(open(\"/tmp/obench-cell-5s01n37h/bench_opencode_regex-chess_huwbm710/re.json\")):\n      fen = re.sub(pattern, repl, fen)\n  return fen.split(\"\\n\")\n```\nthis function should return the FEN position for all possible legal next chess positions.\n\nMake the following simplifying assumptions:\n- You will only be shown positions where it is white to move\n- Any promotions will only be made to Queen (assume that underpromotion is not a legal move)\n- You do not need to track the full-move or half-move count\n\nThe input will be provided, as a string like \"<REDACTED_B64> w kq - 0 1\".\nWhen run on this string, your answer must produce the following output:\n\"<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\"\nNote that the final output of the move and halfmove are allowed to be incorrect. So the above is scored properly even though the move numbers are wrong.\n\nWith these exceptions (and only these exceptions) you must implement a fully correct move generator, including:\n- Castling, with proper tracking of castling rights\n- Promotion, except only allow promotion to queen\n- En-passant\n\nThe length of re.json must be under 100,000 [regex, replacement]-pairs long, and under 10 megabytes in total.\n\nYou can look at the provided check.py to verify if your solution is correct. You will be tested on other positions as well.\n"], "completed": true, "concurrent_cells_at_end": 1, "concurrent_cells_at_start": 4, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 0, "embedded_version": "2.0.50", "ended_et": "2026-11-13T00:45:55.150345-05:00", "ended_on_rejection": false, "endpoint_location": "global", "endpoint_location_mixed": false, "env_cause": null, "env_failure": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "failure_subclass": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "final_workspace_bytes": 412832, "final_workspace_skip_reason": null, "final_workspace_status": "saved", "final_workspace_tar": "/h2/drift-5140-1103/opus/5140/transcripts/without/opencode_regex-chess_claude-opus-5-5_trial1.workspace.tar.gz", "final_workspace_tar_bytes": 32598, "final_workspace_tar_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "free_disk_gb": 35.36, "fresh_subagents": 0, "functional_pass": null, "gate_cell": false, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170344 (/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "<HOST>", "image_digest": null, "image_scan_copies": [], "installed_anthropic": "2.0.50", "instance_id": "8187537343833955709", "instruction_app_rewrite": true, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "load_proof": "pass", "load_proof_basis": "user_agent", "load_proof_reason": "User-Agent 2.0.50", "loaded_anthropic": "2.0.50", "lock_wait_s": 0.0, "lockfile": "bun.lock", "lockfile_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "machine": "<HOST>", "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_match_reason": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "network_mode": "local", "off_protocol": false, "opencode_cache": "/h1/opencode-src", "output_tail": "sant square.\n2. **List candidate moves.** There is one rule for each possible from/to move per piece type: rook/queen and bishop/queen slides with clear-path checks, knights, king steps, pawn pushes and captures, double pushes, en passant and queen-only promotion. Each rule that fits adds a new line with that move made.\n   - **Castling** is only added if the right is still held, the squares between are empty, and the king's square and the square it passes over aren't attacked.\n3. **Remove illegal moves.** Any candidate that leaves the white king attacked by a black piece is deleted.\n4. **Update castling rights.** A right is dropped once its king or rook is no longer on its home square, whether it moved or was captured.\n5. **Rebuild the FEN.** Each line goes back to FEN text with black to move, and the move counters are always written as `0 1`.\n\n**En passant:** after a double push, the output shows the en-passant square only if a black pawn sits next to the pawn that moved. `python-chess` goes further and shows it only when the capture is actually legal. In the rare case where they differ, `check.py` still accepts the answer because it also accepts `-` in that field.\n\n**Testing:** I compared the output against `python-chess` on about 18,000 white-to-move positions, all of which matched. They came from random games, from standard test positions (such as Kiwipete), and from setups built to exercise castling through or out of check, en passant, and promotions with and without captures.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- **No legal moves:** for checkmate or stalemate positions the output is a single empty string rather than an empty list, because of how `split` behaves. The provided test never feeds in such a position.\n- **Speed:** each position takes about 0.4 s. Almost all of that is Python compiling the 2,470 patterns; actually running them takes about 0.04 s.\n\n`test.py`, my comparison script, is also still in the folder, so you can delete it and `gen.py` if you only want `re.json`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "pin_source": "override", "pin_source_class": "override", "probe_method": "embedded", "protocol_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "provider_loaded_mismatch": null, "provider_loaded_source": "embedded", "provider_loaded_version": "2.0.50", "provider_pin_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "provider_trace": "off", "provider_version_proven": true, "provider_version_source": "embedded", "provider_versions": {"@ai-sdk/anthropic": "2.0.50"}, "proxy_cost_usd": 1.2968532000000002, "proxy_observed": [{"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoni